# Warbull — a cyber-minotaur: a bull-headed brute of flesh with machinery
# bolted INTO it (spec: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-27-warbull-design.md).
#
# THIS IS MINOTAUR.BLOB, SCALED 1.28, MINUS ITS PAINTED METAL. The minotaur
# was fitted to a reference mesh (docs/dev-notes/refs/minotaur-mesh/
# minotaur.glb) over six rounds, so its flesh (the V-taper, the trap shelf,
# the bull head, the horns) has a source for every number. Its weak point was
# the hard surface: the prosthetic leg was SDF `box` plates PAINTED metal, and
# the owner's verdict was that they never read as metal (TASKS X2). So this
# file keeps the flesh and throws the paint away: every hard part now lives
# in characters/warbull-kit.wam as real polygons with real metal materials.
#
# THE ONE FACTOR:
#   S  1.28  everything with a length: root height, bone len, clavicle and
#            hip side, r, r2, blend, offset/tip/bend, groove depth/width and
#            the face block's lengths. Angles and bone fractions verbatim.
#            1.90 m authored -> 2.432 m; horn tips 2.033 -> 2.60 m, which
#            keeps 0.4 m of headroom under the rooms' 3.0 m ceilings
#            (game-level.ts WALL_H) for his stride bob. 1.30 would put the
#            tips at 2.64 m; 1.28 is the round number under that.
#            He stands a head over the 2.29 m juggernaut.
#
# THE INLINE COMMENTS QUOTE THE MINOTAUR'S NUMBERS where they explain a
# measurement ("mesh x 1.5612", "tail 1.386"): multiply by 1.28 to get the
# values below. The measurement history itself is in minotaur.blob; if its
# flesh is ever refitted, re-derive this file from it rather than letting
# the two drift.
#
# WHAT CHANGED BEYOND THE SCALE (each marked WARBULL below):
#   - DROPPED: the right-leg prosthetic (five painted `box` plates, a painted
#     cable and two seam grooves) and the painted shoulder cables. Both legs
#     are flesh now; the kit puts hooves, knee cops and pistons on them.
#     The paw claws went too: the kit's hoof encloses the paw.
#   - The horn SWEEP is LEFT-ONLY. His right horn is sawn off at the root
#     and replaced by a steel one in the kit; the flesh root boss stays on
#     both sides so the steel horn has a socket to sit in.
#   - The glowing eye bead is LEFT-ONLY. His right eye is the kit's optic.
#   - A HUMP: a bull's muscle mound behind the neck, which is also the mount
#     for the kit's spine rack. The minotaur's traps sit either side of the
#     neck; nothing filled the back of it.
model warbull
  height 2.432
  # Checked, not decorative: the minotaur's wide semi-crouch, knees forward.
  stance humanoid

skeleton
  # Minotaur rig x 1.28 (see minotaur.blob for why the root sits high in
  # the belly and the clavicles rise at tilt 32).
  root pelvis at 1.11488 len=0.154112
  bone spine1 parent=pelvis dir=up pitch=2 len=0.154112
  bone chest  parent=spine1 dir=up pitch=2 len=0.154112
  bone spine2 parent=chest  dir=up pitch=1 len=0.061952
  bone neck   parent=spine2 dir=up pitch=0 len=0.136064
  # LONG ON PURPOSE (minotaur.blob, "bonewalker's pattern"): the face block
  # rides skull at=0.45, so the length places the cranium, not a joint.
  bone skull  parent=neck   dir=up pitch=0 len=1.0752

  mirror
    bone clavicle parent=neck    side=0.11136 dir=side tilt=32 len=0.384512
    # Arms rest down-and-out: a heavy powerlifter spread.
    bone upperarm parent=clavicle dir=down tilt=40 pitch=8  len=0.391552
    bone forearm  parent=upperarm dir=down tilt=18 pitch=20 len=0.448128
    bone hand     parent=forearm  dir=down tilt=10 pitch=15 len=0.1792
    # The minotaur's wide semi-crouch: hip->knee out and forward, shin
    # swinging back.
    bone thigh    parent=pelvis side=0.22464 dir=down tilt=13.5 pitch=13  len=0.509952
    bone shin     parent=thigh  dir=down tilt=12 pitch=-22                 len=0.564224
    bone foot     parent=shin   dir=fwd                                    len=0.26816
  end

body
  # ============================================================
  # TORSO — the minotaur's V-taper brawler x 1.28. Its rounds 3-6 fitted
  # these against the mesh's rings, silhouette and a front-wall relief map;
  # the numbers and the reasons are in minotaur.blob.
  # ============================================================
  # Pelvis / hip bowl.
  blob torso on pelvis  at=0.50 r=0.17882 wide=1.392 tall=1.30 deep=1.470 blend=0.01536 offset=(-0.023,0,-0.1459) core
  # Waist -> belly: depth pulled in against the chest (the V-taper).
  bar  torso on spine1  from=0.00 to=1.50 r=0.1984 wide=1.490 deep=1.210 blend=0.01536 offset=(0,0,0.0384)
  # Ribcage: a broad flat-fronted slab, width pinned at the judged ceiling
  # (wider rendered as a mushroom).
  bar  torso on chest   from=0.30 to=2.50 r=0.192 wide=1.700 deep=1.430 blend=0.01664 offset=(0,0.0064,0.0128)
  # Trap shelf either side of the neck.
  blob torso on neck    at=0.90 r=0.2432 wide=1.90 tall=1.50 deep=1.30 blend=0.01408 both offset=(0.2074,0.0512,-0.0128)
  # WARBULL: THE HUMP. A bull's muscle mound behind the neck, on the
  # centreline, BETWEEN and behind the trap pair. Sized to rise above the
  # trap shelf's back surface so it reads in profile, and set behind the neck
  # so it never swells the throat (the minotaur's worst relief-map cell was
  # a throat filled by the traps). It is the base the kit's spine rack is
  # bolted to, so it must be flesh: the rack's flange bites into it.
  blob torso on neck    at=0.55 r=0.2000 wide=1.35 tall=1.10 deep=1.20 blend=0.02000 offset=(0,0.030,-0.1700)

  # MUSCLE RELIEF (the minotaur's round 6): pec pair, lower-pec shelf,
  # sternum, upper-ab mass, linea alba, ab cross-lines, obliques. Engine
  # limited today (the AO term cannot see relief this shallow, TASKS X4);
  # kept because the masses improved the form and the grooves are free.
  blob torso on neck   at=0.72 offset=(0.1254,0,0.1638) r=0.13824 wide=1.30 tall=1.15 deep=0.62 blend=0.00768 both
  groove torso on neck at=0.30 offset=(0.1152,0,0.192) r=0.1472 wide=1.39 tall=0.05 depth=0.0192 width=0.00045 both
  groove torso on neck at=0.60 offset=(0,0,0.2176) r=0.128 wide=0.05 tall=1.50 depth=0.02816 width=0.00038
  bar  torso on chest  from=0.85 to=1.75 r=0.192 wide=1.79 deep=1.66 blend=0.0128 offset=(0,0,0.0256)
  groove torso on spine1 at=1.10 offset=(0,0,0.2432) r=0.1152 wide=0.05 tall=1.60 depth=0.01536 width=0.00032
  groove torso on spine1 at=1.35 offset=(0,0,0.2368) r=0.1664 wide=1.25 tall=0.05 depth=0.01664 width=0.00038
  groove torso on spine1 at=0.95 offset=(0,0,0.2368) r=0.1664 wide=1.25 tall=0.05 depth=0.01664 width=0.00038
  blob torso on spine1 at=0.10 offset=(0.2061,0,0.0896) r=0.12928 wide=0.95 tall=1.39 deep=1.10 blend=0.01024 both

  # Neck: a short bar swallowed by the traps, fusing head -> torso.
  bar  head on neck from=-0.30 to=1.20 r=0.0768 deep=1.20 blend=0.00768

  # ============================================================
  # HORNS. Root bosses at the temple/crown corner, both sides: the left one
  # grows the flesh horn, the right one is the socket the kit's steel horn
  # is collared into.
  # ============================================================
  blob head on skull at=0.58 offset=(0.1254,0,0.0256) r=0.0704 wide=1.0 tall=0.85 deep=1.0 blend=0.0064 both color=6e4426
  # WARBULL: the wrapped sweep on the LEFT only (+x; a head prim without
  # `both` is placed exactly where its offset says). Leaves the skull
  # sideways and hooks up at the tip (the bend pulls the curve out and down
  # of the chord); tip at ~2.60 m.
  bar  head on skull from=0.575 to=0.70 offset=(0.1254,0,0.0256) tip=(0.2074,0.0589,-0.0064) bend=(0.0614,-0.0538,0) r=0.064 r2=0.01664 blend=0.00512 chamfer color=221a1a gloss=0.45

  # WARBULL: the glowing eye bead on the LEFT only. The right eye socket is
  # the kit's optic housing. Placement: the minotaur's decal-solve eye row,
  # sunk to ~60% depth (minotaur.blob, EYES).
  blob head on skull at=0.41 offset=(0.0448,0,0.2342) r=0.01536 blend=0.00512 color=ff2200 glow=0.9

  # ============================================================
  # ARMS — huge. Deltoid ball is the arm's core (the fuse probe must not
  # pick an accessory). The RIGHT forearm is flesh on purpose: the
  # launcher (a held prop, like the juggernaut's chaingun) swallows the fist
  # and the lower forearm, and the kit bolts a socket collar at the elbow.
  # ============================================================
  blob arm on clavicle at=1.00 r=0.1728 blend=0.01024 mirror core
  bar  arm on upperarm from=0.00 to=0.95 r=0.13952 r2=0.14336 wide=1.000 blend=0.00768 mirror offset=(0,0.0013,0.0051)
  bar  arm on forearm  from=0.00 to=0.90 r=0.1408 r2=0.1015 deep=1.078 tall=1.131 blend=0.00768 mirror offset=(0,-0.0013,-0.0102)
  blob arm on hand     at=0.45 r=0.1088 wide=0.95 tall=1.10 deep=1.25 blend=0.0064 mirror

  # ============================================================
  # LEGS — both flesh now (WARBULL: the painted prosthetic is gone). The
  # minotaur's left-leg fit, mirrored: muscled thigh, calf bulge behind,
  # thick ankle, splayed beast paw. WARBULL: the paw's two claw prims are
  # dropped; the kit's steel-shod hoof encloses the paw and IS the foot now
  # (its back third stays out behind the hoof as a fleshy fetlock).
  # ============================================================
  blob leg on thigh at=0.02 r=0.2048 blend=0.01024 mirror core
  bar  leg on thigh from=0.05 to=0.92 r=0.14989 r2=0.21363 wide=1.02 blend=0.00896 mirror offset=(0,-0.0269,-0.0666)
  blob leg on shin  at=0.02 r=0.16 deep=0.95 blend=0.00896 mirror
  bar  leg on shin  from=0.08 to=0.60 r=0.1385 r2=0.14784 deep=1.216 tall=1.0 blend=0.00896 mirror offset=(0,-0.0026,-0.0282)
  bar  leg on shin  from=0.60 to=0.98 r=0.03891 r2=0.16858 blend=0.00768 mirror offset=(0,0.0115,-0.0768)
  blob leg on foot  at=0.30 offset=(0.0128,-0.0691,0.1216) r=0.11853 wide=1.35 tall=1.07 deep=1.45 blend=0.00768 mirror

# ============================================================
# FACE — the minotaur's head block x 1.28 (lengths only; the ratios are
# verbatim, so the decal projection below lands on the same head-space
# features it was solved for).
# ============================================================
face
  headRadius 0.16
  headWidth  1.00
  headHeight 1.55
  headDepth  1.50
  jawWidth   0.95
  jawHeight  1.00
  jawDrop    0.1664
  jawJut     0.1408
  noseLength 0.0384
  noseWidth  0.80
  noseDrop   0.0384
  browHeavy  0.0205
  browRise   0.0512
  headBlend  0.0064

# Face decal: baked from the minotaur's reference mesh with
#   npm run blob:face-bake -- minotaur --head-frac 0.165
# then cropped with a soft edge to uv.x 0.385..0.615, uv.y 0.28..0.60 (a
# little narrower than the minotaur's recipe, 0.34..0.66, which let the horn
# wraps in at the sides). The minotaur's own PNG was never committed; this
# is the first time that bake exists in the repo. Projection: the
# minotaur's solve verbatim (eye row at hs.y -0.176, fang row at -0.510),
# valid because the head is scaled uniformly.
sheet
  image       warbull-face.png
  decal       1
  projScaleX  0.130
  projScaleY  0.314
  projCentreX 0.5
  projCentreY 0.555

# Palette: the minotaur's (its round 4 retarget onto the zombie's
# henenlotter-latex pink, which read under the lab key where the mesh's
# measured brown was a chocolate mass). Unchanged on purpose for the first
# frames: the chrome kit is new, and flesh-vs-metal contrast is judged with
# both in the picture.
palette
  baseColor     0.86 0.47 0.48
  deepColor     0.74 0.06 0.10
  charColor     0.10 0.07 0.08
  specIntensity 0.95
  specRoughness 0.16
  fresnelBoost  0.75
  translucency  0.45
  surfaceNoiseAmp    0.09
  silhouetteNoiseAmp 0.014
  wetness       0.85
  mottleAmp     0.11
  mottleScale   1.6
  mottleColor   0.62 0.28 0.30
